    "desc": "A program ran a tunnelling, relay or reverse-proxy tool - ngrok, cloudflared, a dev/VSCode tunnel, frp, gost, chisel, bore, or an SSH port-forward (-L/-R/-D/-W). These punch an inbound path through NAT and the firewall to expose a local service or relay traffic (MITRE T1572), which is a classic way to reach a host the egress controls were meant to contain. reverse_shell covers an interactive shell back out; this covers the tunnels and relays.",
